                        <field name="dc_subject">Taxed-Spain-1853 </field>
                        <field name="dc_title">The Hon. Mr. Tomas Moyano, Secretary of State and the Office of Grace and Justice, informed the Council, through the Hon. Mr. Duke of Infantado, President of him... the following order [Printed text]: "Hon. Mr. Secretary of the Office of the Treasury what follows: The King... to the proposal of the Supreme Council of the Treasury, it has been served to send that while he does not consult with the due knowledge the general providence that is more convenient to reintegrate the owners of alcabas, stubs and other enagenated rights of the Crown... is suspended all praise for reason of debts of this nature... </field>
